# Generated beets runtime configs carrying a live Discogs token (WR-04, defence in depth).
# scripts/spike03-gen-import-config.sh REFUSES to write inside any git working tree, and that
# refusal is the real control. This is the second net, for a bypass of it or a hand-rolled copy:
# the token is in the file as `discogs: user_token:`, the repo is PUBLIC, and `git log -S` keeps
# a committed credential recoverable long after it is deleted.
#
# Deliberately NARROW - it names the generated file, not `*config*.yaml`, so it cannot mask a
# legitimate tracked config such as stacks/selfhosted/music/wrtag.yaml or a stack's config.yaml.
# The real artefact is /mnt/fast/spike-03/beets-config/import-xcheck.yaml (03-DISCOGS-EVIDENCE.md
# § Screening); both its bare name and its beets-config/ parent are covered, because a bypass
# would most likely be a copy of the whole directory into the checkout.
import-xcheck.yaml
**/beets-config/*.yaml

# Python bytecode. scripts/normalise-dj-tags.py (plan 03-05) is this repo's first committed
# Python file, and its own verification command is `python3 -m py_compile`, which drops a
# __pycache__/ directory beside it. Ignored so a verification run cannot dirty the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
